  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KAI - Sand Survey in the Nile Delta Offshore Zone</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is to conduct a geophysical survey in the Nile Delta Offshore Zone to determine and inform the Egyptian government about the resources of minable sand of suitable quality in the Nile delta offshore zone in order to make a well-informed decision on the feasibility of a climate adaptation strategy for the Nile delta coast that is based on coastal sand nourishments.
The outcome consist of 2D and 3D maps showing the presence of sand resources accompanied by volume calculations.
The results will be used by the EGY Ministry of Water Resources and Irrigation (MWRI), specifically the Shore Protection Authority (SPA), and Invest International for the Feasibility Studies on specific locations where sand nourishment could be applied in future. 
Rijkswaterstaat will provide TA (funded separately by BOA or the Partners for Water programme) to build SPA&apos;s capacities.</narrative>
  </description>
